      "sequence_position": 1,
      "problem": "Write the equation of the hyperbola $7{x}^{2}-4{y}^{2}=56$ in standard form.",
      "worked_solution": "The Cartesian equation of a horizontal hyperbola centered at the origin is\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, to write the equation of the hyperbola in standard form, we need to divide both sides of the equation by $56$ and then simplify, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}7{x}^{2}-4{y}^{2} & =56 \\\\ \\frac{7{x}^{2}}{56}-\\frac{4{y}^{2}}{56} & =\\frac{56}{56} \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{8}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{14} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$",
